{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>A life for a life</b> in the case of an animal is not literal, such that he would need to acquire for him an animal like his animal, but rather that he pay him money in the amount of the damage he caused him. And likewise, \"fracture for fracture, eye for eye\" (Leviticus 24:20) is according to the opinion of our Sages (Bava Kamma 83)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:59:06.191240013Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}